  "rules": [
    "Building volume: up to 15–20% a week is fine while you return to volumes you've already handled (up to about 85 km). Beyond that, 5–10% a week. Never add more than about 25 km in one week: your jump from 41 to 116 km in August came five weeks before the ankle pain that cut a long run short.",
    "No empty weeks: the dashboard shows 10 weeks under 15 km in the last year. Unless you're ill or injured, keep every week above 50 km, even when travelling, using shorter runs if needed.",
    "Hamstring and ankle: stop a session if pain is sharp or changes how you run. Take 2–3 easy days, and see a physio if it isn't clearly better within a week.",
    "Missed training: under 4 days, carry on as planned. One week missed, repeat the previous week. Two weeks or more, drop back two weeks in the plan.",
    "Illness: symptoms only above the neck, run easy. Fever or chest symptoms, rest completely.",
    "Shoes: Alphaflys for marathon-pace long runs, key sessions and races only. Everything else in your trainers, rotating two pairs once you pass 90 km a week.",
    "Sleep and fuel: 7–9 hours of sleep, and a carbohydrate-rich meal within an hour of every long run and hard session.",
    "Check the dashboard every few weeks: your Running progression review shows whether the weekly bars are steady and how many long runs you've done."
  ],
